TITLE:: Deken
summary:: Find, install, update and remove SuperCollider plugins and quarks
categories:: Quarks
related:: Guides/Deken-Guide, Classes/DekenGui, Classes/Quarks

DESCRIPTION::
Deken is a package manager for SuperCollider plugins (UGens) and quarks. It
finds packages in a signed package list, installs prebuilt plugins (or builds
them on this computer when there is no prebuilt version), and installs quarks
for you.

For a walk through the window with pictures, see link::Guides/Deken-Guide::.

The work is done by a small helper program, code::scdeken::. The first time
you use Deken it is downloaded, checked against a checksum that ships with the
quark, and kept in the sc-deken folder inside link::Classes/Platform#*userAppSupportDir::.

All methods are asynchronous. They return at once, the interpreter keeps
running, and the result arrives later. Pass an code::action:: function to get the
result; without one, a readable summary is posted.

subsection:: The response
code::action:: is called with an Event:

definitionlist::
## ok || true when it worked.
## data || the answer, as parsed JSON: Dictionaries with String keys, Arrays, Strings, numbers, Booleans.
## error || in plain words, when ok is false.
## confirm || what still needs the user's OK: code::"unreviewed"::, code::"retracted":: or code::"duplicates"::.
## needsConfirmation || true when an install is waiting for the user's answer (see link::#*install::).
## after_install || after an install: code::"recompile":: and/or code::"reboot-server"::.
## exit_code || the helper's exit code (0 ok, 1 error, 3 needs confirmation).
::

subsection:: What the helper may touch
Plugin packages go into code::<user extension folder>/sc-deken/<name>::. Quarks are
installed by SuperCollider itself (link::Classes/Quarks::). Nothing you own is deleted
without asking: replaced copies are moved to a backup folder.

CLASSMETHODS::

private:: prSimple, prRequest, prLog, prProgress, prNeeded, prFindItem, prRemoveQuark, prInstallQuarks, prInstallQuark, prAfterInstall, prDefaultAction, prPostFailure, prPostSearch, prPostList, prPostInstall, prPostConfirmation

subsection:: Finding packages

METHOD:: platform
Shows which computer, SuperCollider version and plugin API sc-deken sees. Prebuilt plugins are chosen by this.
ARGUMENT:: action
Function called with the response. code::data:: has code::os::, code::arch::, code::api::, code::sc_version:: and code::key::.
code::
Deken.platform;
Deken.platform({ |r| r.data["key"].postln });
::

METHOD:: search
Looks for packages by name, summary, UGen or class name.
ARGUMENT:: query
Text to look for.
ARGUMENT:: kind
code::nil:: for all, or code::"plugin"::, code::"quark"::, code::"plugin+quark"::.
ARGUMENT:: includeUnreviewed
Also list packages nobody has reviewed yet. Default false.
ARGUMENT:: action
Function called with the response. code::data:: is an Array of hits with code::name::, code::kind::, code::trust::, code::latest:: and code::summary::.
code::
Deken.search("pitch");
Deken.search("fm", "plugin", action: { |r| r.data.do { |h| h["name"].postln } });
::

METHOD:: info
Everything the package list knows about one package: versions, trust, dependencies and withdrawn versions.
ARGUMENT:: name
Package name.
ARGUMENT:: action
Function called with the response.
code::
Deken.info(\Panola);
::

METHOD:: list
Packages installed on this computer (through sc-deken, as quarks, or by hand) with their versions.
ARGUMENT:: action
Function called with the response; code::data:: is an Array.
code::
Deken.list;
::

METHOD:: updates
Like link::#*list::, but only what has a newer version.
ARGUMENT:: action
Function called with the response.
code::
Deken.updates;
::

METHOD:: doctor
Checks the tools needed to build plugins on this computer (compiler, CMake, git). Give a package name to check what that package needs.
ARGUMENT:: name
Package name, or code::nil:: for the general check.
ARGUMENT:: action
Function called with the response.
code::
Deken.doctor;
Deken.doctor(\fmx6);
::

METHOD:: refresh
Downloads the package list again instead of using the saved copy.
ARGUMENT:: action
Function called with the response.
code::
Deken.refresh;
::

METHOD:: plan
Works out how a package would be installed (prebuilt, built here, or as a quark), and what would need your OK, without installing anything.
ARGUMENT:: name
Package name.
ARGUMENT:: version
Version, or code::nil:: for the newest.
ARGUMENT:: action
Function called with the response; code::data:: is the plan.

METHOD:: advisories
Lists installed packages that a security notice has withdrawn.
ARGUMENT:: action
Function called with the response; code::data:: is an Array.

METHOD:: quarantineClear
Permanently deletes the packages that were put in quarantine. Ask first: this cannot be undone.
ARGUMENT:: action
Function called with the response.

METHOD:: gui
Opens the package manager window: browse and search with the type and one-line summary of each package, see what is installed, what has updates, the build log, and the settings. See link::Classes/DekenGui::.
code::
Deken.gui;
::

subsection:: Installing and removing

METHOD:: install
Installs a package and the packages it needs. Plugins are placed in the managed extension folder; quarks are installed by sclang. If something needs your OK first (an unreviewed package, a withdrawn version, an existing copy of the same plugin), nothing is installed. The action gets the plan with code::needsConfirmation:: true and code::confirm:: listing what is needed; the posted message shows the exact link::#*installConfirmed:: call to make if you agree.
ARGUMENT:: name
Package name.
ARGUMENT:: version
Version to install, or code::nil:: for the newest.
ARGUMENT:: action
Function called with the response.
code::
Deken.install(\Panola);
Deken.install(\fmx6, nil, { |r|
    if(r[\needsConfirmation] == true) { ("needs: " ++ r.confirm).postln } { r.ok.postln };
});
::

METHOD:: installConfirmed
Installs after you have answered the questions.
ARGUMENT:: name
Package name.
ARGUMENT:: version
Version, or code::nil:: for the newest.
ARGUMENT:: choices
An Event with your answers: code::confirm_unreviewed:: (true), code::confirm_retracted:: (true), code::on_duplicate:: (code::"replace":: or code::"keep"::).
ARGUMENT:: action
Function called with the response. When it finishes, a message says whether to recompile the class library and reboot the server.
code::
Deken.installConfirmed(\somePackage, nil, (confirm_unreviewed: true));
::

METHOD:: update
Installs the newest version of a package. An installed quark is moved to the new version (with link::Classes/Quarks::); plugins are replaced and the old copy is kept in the backup folder.
ARGUMENT:: name
Package name.
ARGUMENT:: action
Function called with the response. Asks for confirmation like link::#*install::.
code::
Deken.update(\Panola);
::

METHOD:: remove
Removes a package installed through sc-deken, or uninstalls a quark.
ARGUMENT:: name
Package name.
ARGUMENT:: action
Function called with the response.
code::
Deken.remove(\fmx6);
::

subsection:: Settings

METHOD:: helperPath
Developers: use this scdeken program instead of the downloaded one. code::nil:: (the default) downloads and checks the released helper.
code::
Deken.helperPath = "C:/dev/sc-deken/scdeken.exe";
::

METHOD:: indexURL
Use another package list (address or code::file:///:: URL; a signature file with the same name plus code::.minisig:: must sit next to it and be made with a key listed in code::trusted-keys.txt::). code::nil:: uses the official list.
code::
Deken.indexURL = "file:///C:/test/index.json";
::

METHOD:: logAction
A function called with each log line the helper sends while it works, instead of posting it. A graphical interface can show these.
code::
Deken.logAction = { |line| line.postln };
::

METHOD:: progressAction
A function called with code::(fraction, label):: while the helper works (fraction goes from 0 to 1).
code::
Deken.progressAction = { |fraction, label| "% %".format(label, (fraction * 100).asInteger).postln };
::

EXAMPLES::
code::
// Find a package, then install it.
Deken.search("fm");
Deken.install(\fmx6);

// Afterwards: Language > Recompile Class Library, then s.reboot.
::
